<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Ablation Studies</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we rigorously dissect the design choices for the continuous unified representation <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{z}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We select SigLIP2-SO400M-Patch16-NaFlex <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tschannen et al. (2025)</a></cite> features as the foundation due to their dense features for improved semantic understanding. However, directly modeling such high-dimensional representations is challenging. Therefore, we investigate how to efficiently compress these features from two perspectives: (1) Optimal Feature Shape (sequence vs. dimension compression), and (2) Projector Architecture (mlp vs. attention).</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.3.1 </span>Optimal Feature Shape</h4>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first determine the optimal shape for the compressed representation space <math id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math> by varying the sequence length <math id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and feature dimension <math id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>.
We control the sequence length <math id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> via the maximum token count and the dimension <math id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> via a learnable mlp bottleneck (compressor and decompressor).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reducing dimensions maintains higher reconstruction fidelity than reducing sequence length.</span>
As shown in Tab <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 4.3.1 Optimal Feature Shape ‣ 4.3 Ablation Studies ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ UniCom: Unified Multimodal Modeling via Compressed Continuous Semantic Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and Fig <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Diffusion Decoder. ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ UniCom: Unified Multimodal Modeling via Compressed Continuous Semantic Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, original siglip features yield excellent reconstruction fidelity (rFID 0.40). However, reduce sequence length drastically undermines image quality. In contrast, dimension reduction via MLP, whether compressing to 256 or 64 dimensions, results in relatively minimal performance loss.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reducing dimensions yields superior image generation performance than reducing sequence length.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:39%;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Reconstruction performance of different compressed feature shapes on ImageNet50k <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deng et al., 2009</a>)</cite>.</figcaption>
