</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>More Results of Image Editing</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present comprehensive qualitative results to demonstrate the versatility of UniCom across diverse image editing and generation scenarios, spanning single-image editing (<a href="#A5.F13" title="In Intelligent Image Editing. ‣ Appendix E More Results of Image Editing ‣ UniCom: Unified Multimodal Modeling via Compressed Continuous Semantic Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>), multi-element composition (<a href="#A5.F14" title="In Intelligent Image Editing. ‣ Appendix E More Results of Image Editing ‣ UniCom: Unified Multimodal Modeling via Compressed Continuous Semantic Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>), and knowledge-driven intelligent editing (<a href="#A5.F15" title="In Intelligent Image Editing. ‣ Appendix E More Results of Image Editing ‣ UniCom: Unified Multimodal Modeling via Compressed Continuous Semantic Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Single Image Editing.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A5.F13" title="In Intelligent Image Editing. ‣ Appendix E More Results of Image Editing ‣ UniCom: Unified Multimodal Modeling via Compressed Continuous Semantic Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> illustrates the broad editing capabilities of UniCom across six representative tasks: (1) <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Add/Remove/Extract</span>, which covers adding objects, removing elements, and extracting subjects from scenes; (2) <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Replace</span>, which substitutes objects or materials while faithfully preserving contextual layout; (3) <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Style Transfer</span>, which transforms image appearance into various artistic styles; (4) <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Background</span>, which modifies or replaces image backgrounds; (5) <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Subject-Driven Generation</span>, which generates new images conditioned on reference subjects; and (6) <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Controllable Generation</span>, which produces images guided by spatial or structural control signals. These results confirm that our compressed continuous semantic representation retains sufficient fine-grained information to enable precise, instruction-following edits.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Multi-Element Composition.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A5.F14" title="In Intelligent Image Editing. ‣ Appendix E More Results of Image Editing ‣ UniCom: Unified Multimodal Modeling via Compressed Continuous Semantic Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> demonstrates the ability of UniCom to compose multiple reference subjects into a coherent scene. Despite the challenge of maintaining the identity of each element while harmonizing spatial arrangement and stylistic consistency, our model produces visually plausible compositions. This capability benefits from the rich semantic priors preserved by the channel-compressed representation, enabling faithful identity preservation even without relying on VAE-based reconstruction.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Intelligent Image Editing.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Beyond conventional instruction-based editing, we further evaluate UniCom on benchmarks that require world knowledge and contextual reasoning, namely WorldEdit <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. (2026)</a></cite> and Kris <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2025d)</a></cite>. Unlike systems that rely on explicit editing commands, these benchmarks require models to integrate world knowledge priors and perform reasoning over semantic representations before generating the desired output. <a href="#A5.F15" title="In Intelligent Image Editing. ‣ Appendix E More Results of Image Editing ‣ UniCom: Unified Multimodal Modeling via Compressed Continuous Semantic Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> showcases representative examples that involve biological transformations, geographical understanding, and cultural context. Rather than following literal instructions, the model must infer what transformation is semantically appropriate given the input, which highlights the advantage of unifying understanding and generation within a shared semantic space.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Quantitatively, as shown in <a href="#A5.T7" title="In Intelligent Image Editing. ‣ Appendix E More Results of Image Editing ‣ UniCom: Unified Multimodal Modeling via Compressed Continuous Semantic Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, UniCom achieves a high overall score of 4.35/5 on WorldEdit-Test, demonstrating strong performance across diverse cause categories. These results underscore the effectiveness of semantic representation for generation: by leveraging rich visual-language priors, UniCom produces more coherent and contextually accurate edits, outperforming most traditional methods that rely solely on explicit instructions. The integration of world knowledge and reasoning significantly enhances the model’s ability to handle complex and context-sensitive editing tasks.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>The performance of both commercial and open-source models on image editing tasks in WorldEdit-Test, evaluated across different causes and metrics.</figcaption>
<div id="A5.T7.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:281pt;vertical-align:-139.5pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-260.8pt,212.5pt) scale(0.398108111720061,0.398108111720061) ;">
<table id="A5.T7.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
